Found under k320 (choices worker, 2026-10-31): `ocp node add --gpu` reads Config::gpu_enabled only after the node has joined and is Ready, outside an eval. Since k320 a malformed gpu.enabled (e.g. `no`) makes the command die there -- after the join, with the node in the cluster. Before k320 it read the string as on and rolled the GPU stack out.

Fix: read the GPU switches (or the relevant part of validate()) before the join, so a malformed ocp.yaml stops `ocp node add` before it touches the machine. Related: k306 (commands that read the spec without validate()), k309 (Node/Add.pm).

Done = a malformed gpu switch stops `ocp node add --gpu` before any SSH/join step, with validate()'s line on STDERR (test).

2026-10-31 12:00 Worked in scratch copies on f276d35 (shared tree untouched). Decision: ocp node add --gpu (without --nowait) checks only validate()'s gpu:/gpu.* lines, all at once, as the first thing after the option checks -- before _k8s (PIN1), the provider lookup, the OCPNode write, the SSH probe (PIN2) and the join. Not all of validate() as k321 (node add reads little else of ocp.yaml; a cilium:/lbipam: line would hold a node up over something it never reads), not only gpu.enabled (gpu.driver/toolkit/amd.* and, since k331, unknown gpu keys fail the GPU steps after the join too). Not with --nowait (reads none of the block; ocp apply refuses the same lines, k255). control_planes/workers shapes stay k306's. Red on base: t/333 16/33 failed (full run incl. join, then the croak at Add.pm line 888).

